AI assistance
I used AI assistants (large language models) to search the literature, write and review code, and draft documentation. I defined the problem, chose the data, assumptions and scope, and checked the outputs against the cited sources. Agronomic validation with local growers or agronomists is still pending.

Data
- NASA POWER (Prediction Of Worldwide Energy Resources), daily point API v2.10.3.
- NASA Harmonized Landsat and Sentinel-2 (HLS) v2.0, distributed by NASA LP DAAC.
- NASA EMIT L2B Estimated Fractional Cover v002 (DOI 10.5067/EMIT/EMITL2BFRCOV.002), distributed by NASA LP DAAC. Landsat data courtesy of NASA/USGS; contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data (ESA).
- NOAA NCEI Global Surface Summary of the Day (GSOD), station 87715099999.
- ESA WorldCover 10 m 2021 v200, CC BY 4.0.
- Gerencia de Catastro – Agencia de Recaudación Tributaria, Provincia de Río Negro (IDERN WFS geonode:PARCELARIO1). Public provincial parcel layer; boundaries shown and published as served in public/data/parcel_outlines.json and study_parcels.json, with attribution. The original GeoJSON is not redistributed (obtained with scripts/fetch_parcelario.py). No formal licence text found; these data are not covered by the MIT licence of the code.

- Weather forecast: Open-Meteo (open-meteo.com), CC BY 4.0, free non-commercial use, requested live by the browser (and by the optional API's /api/weather route).
- Read-only API: Cloudflare Worker serving the processed files above; no third-party data beyond those listed.
- Map backgrounds, loaded live and never bundled: EOxCloudless 2024 by EOX IT Services GmbH (contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2024), CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; NASA GIBS (HLS); © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).
- Logo: AI-generated image, marked "Logo: AI-generated" where it is shown (see docs/AI_DISCLOSURE.md). Map library: Leaflet (BSD-2-Clause).

Fonts (bundled via @fontsource): Fraunces and IBM Plex Sans / Mono, SIL Open Font License 1.1.
